ed_at":null,"archived_by":null}],"state":"closed","locked":false,"assignees":[],"milestone":null,"comments":3,"created_at":"2026-02-09T10:06:50Z","updated_at":"2026-02-09T12:53:02Z","closed_at":"2026-02-09T10:19:02Z","assignee":null,"author_association":"NONE","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"### Tested versions\n\nGodot 4.5.1.stable\n\n### System information\n\nWindows 11 - Godot.4.5.1.stable\n\n### Issue description\n\nI have created a model in blender with two animations, Walk and Draw Bow.\n\nWalk does not move the spine at all, just the hips.\nBow Draw does not move the hips, nor the spine.\nOn their own they play fine, and show no wobble in the upper body.\n\nWhenever I use a Blend2 node to combine these animations, with an applied filter from the spine up, the Bow Draw animations starts to wobble from the hips up. \n\nThis is kind of unexpected to me, as neither of the animations move the spine. This looks like a typical case for animation blending to me, and it gets me scratching my head too much to figure it out.\n\nI've also experimented with the Add2 node, which adds animations but this would mean I would not be able to use the hands. Is this the correct way to blend animations?\n\n\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\nCreate two animations with legs moving in one, and arms moving in another.\nBlend then animations with the AnimationTree using Blend2 node.\n\n### Minimal reproduction project (MRP)\n\n[animation_bug_2026-02-09_11-01-36.zip](https://github.com/user-attachments/files/25180090/animation_bug_2026-02-09_11-01-36.zip)","closed_by":{"login":"TokageItLab","id":61938263,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYxOTM4MjYz","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/61938263?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab","html_url":"https://g